module v3.std.services

import std.types { HttpMethod }
import std.effects { PathTemplate }

// PR-α — service / operation / REST-endpoint substrate carrier types.
//
// Type-authority pass only. No `data` rows here; `bootstrap_fixture_authority`
// (`src/v3/std/extdeps_bootstrap_fixtures.dag`) is unchanged in this PR.
// Sibling fixture rows of shape `data <provider>_operations: List<Operation>`
// (anthropic / openai / github) are PR-β..ω scope, owned by R2 Grounding Manager
// (T-Ground-Services analog of T-Ground-LanguageSpec — see #1195 for the
// `MethodTemplateContract` precedent these carriers mirror in shape and cadence).
//
// **Path-structure authority is upstream.** This file does NOT define
// path-template structure; it imports `PathTemplate` from `std.effects`
// (`src/v3/std/effects.dag:142`), which carries the
// `UrlPathToken = LiteralToken{text} | ParamToken{name}` flat-token shape
// staged from `dsl/std/http_path.dag` (RFC 6570 Level 1 substitution). That
// flat-token shape is the only single-authority shape capable of representing
// mixed parameter/literal segments such as `{secret_name}:addVersion` (Google
// Cloud convention) without lossy whole-segment coproduct collapse.
// Re-declaring path structure here would create a parallel authority and
// the fidelity gap the `std.http_path` authors specifically avoid.
//
// **Input-field-name uniqueness is by construction.** `Operation.inputs` is
// `Map<String, InputField>` rather than `List<InputField>` so duplicate
// input names are unrepresentable: `Map`'s key invariant carries the
// scope-identity authority. `ParamToken.name` from a path-template token
// resolves into this map's key set; the fail-closed boundary check that
// every `ParamToken.name` is a present key lands at fixture load alongside
// the first `data <provider>_operations` row (PR-β). No separate
// `InputFieldRef` carrier is introduced here, since `ParamToken.name`
// already carries the same shape and adding a wrapper would duplicate
// without strengthening the structural invariant.
//
// Lands without a producerless-carrier complaint by the same argument that
// applied to `MethodTemplateContract` in `emit_model.dag` ahead of Phase 1:
// type declarations are substrate authority; fixture rows are downstream
// population. The dissolution-tracked carrier discipline runs on the
// fixture side, not on the type side.
//
// Downstream consumers (after PR-β..ω land):
//   - `analyze_workflow` / `analyze_parallelism`
//     (`src/v3/compiler/src/workflow_idempotency.rs`,
//     `workflow_parallelism.rs`) derive `OperationEffect` per
//     `std.effects::derive_op_effect(method, path)` from loaded `Operation`
//     records; authored `lane2_workflow` retires.
//   - `OperationEffect` substrate type
//     (`src/v3/compiler/src/dag/effects.rs`, `src/v3/std/effects.dag`)
//     retires once derivation replaces the authored shape — path (ii) of
//     the T-ImpossibleBugs unenumerated-effects design (PR #808 / #971,
//     `docs/briefs/r2-impossible-bugs-unenumerated-effects-worker.md` Q5.5).

// 🟢 TERMINAL at PR-α scope. Per-input-field metadata slot. Empty in PR-α
// because `derive_op_effect` keys path-segment binding by name only and
// does not consume per-field type data today. Reserved as a record so
// PR-β can grow a `ty: …` field (or similar) without changing
// `Operation.inputs`'s map shape. The canonical name is held by the
// enclosing `Map<String, InputField>` key, not duplicated here, which
// keeps single-authority for the input-field name (no `name: String`
// field that could disagree with the map key).
type InputField {}

// 🟢 TERMINAL at PR-α scope. Carries the structural facts
// `std.effects::derive_op_effect(method_str, path_str)` (see `effects.dag`
// line 707) needs to derive `OperationEffect.shape` from a callable's REST
// realization: the HTTP verb, and the path template whose last segment
// drives the create-vs-upsert-vs-delete branch via
// `last_path_param(template)`. `path` reuses the upstream `PathTemplate`
// authority from `std.effects` so mixed parameter/literal segments
// (`{secret_name}:addVersion`) are representable without loss.
//
// Body-shape (which input fields compose into the request body) is not
// modeled here in PR-α. `derive_op_effect` does not consume body shape
// today; if a future shape needs it, extend with a `body_inputs: …`
// field whose entries are validated against `Operation.inputs` keys at
// fixture load (same boundary discipline as `ParamToken.name`).
// Omission preserves the minimal-PR-α scope.
type RestEndpointBinding {
  method: HttpMethod
  path:   PathTemplate
}

// 🟢 TERMINAL at PR-α scope. Named operation plus its REST realization +
// uniquely-keyed input-field map (the latter scoping `ParamToken.name`
// resolution by-construction). The product is `std.effects::OperationEffect`'s
// prerequisite shape: every `OperationEffect.operation_name + endpoint.method
// + endpoint.path` is recoverable from one `Operation`, dissolving the
// parallel-rep that motivates the retirement (T-ImpossibleBugs path (ii)).
type Operation {
  name:     String
  inputs:   Map<String, InputField>
  endpoint: RestEndpointBinding
}
